        {
          "id": 955832841,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The problem for me locally is that I set CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH in my environment in order for CMake to find Qt. I need to build master (preferably with Qt 6) along with 3.6 and 3.4 (which require Qt 5). WIRESHARK_QT6_PREFIX_PATH makes that easier, but it looks like I can use CMakeListsCustom.txt instead.\n\nWe should be able to discover the Qt version by trying `find_package(Qt6 ...)` and if that fails, trying `find_package(Qt5 ...)`. That would let us get rid of USE_qt6.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-05-23T00:54:01.287Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-05-23T00:54:01.287Z",
